That assessment of other people's motivations is *also* parody, whether 
intended to be so or not.

The real issue isn't farming or extinctionism. It's that many people 
have complained that the later game (post-Castle pre-ascension run) is 
*boring,* and it's boring largely because there's nothing to prevent, or 
even to dissuade, players from screwing around buffing up their 
characters to the point where nothing in the game offers any challenge 
anymore. This "screwing around" includes farming and extinctionism, and 
you'll notice that people who engage in them don't talk about what a 
challenge the game is at that point, but how mindlessly tedious it is.

The suggestion for a soft in-game "clock" is merely a suggestion to keep 
the game challenging throughout. The hostility that this suggestion 
engenders is astonishing.

